=== layout: section
# Sex-linked Punnett Square

=== layout: two-panels

# A Punnett square for X-linked inheritance

@left

| Egg / sperm | X | Y |
| --- | --- | --- |
| X | XX | XY |
| X | XX | XY |

@right

Each son receives his X chromosome from his mother and his Y chromosome from his father.

Expected female : male ratio = 1 : 1.

=== layout: two-panels
# Sex-linked Punnett Square

@left

- Based on a Google Images and textbook search, there is [*no consensus*]{underline=true} on where the male and female gamete genotypes go\:
  - Sperm on top\: 33
  - Egg on top\: 20
- Our text seems to prefer male/sperm on top, female/egg on the side.

@right

